    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d427">

                <pb facs="0569" n="501" sameAs="frus:frus1867p1/pg501"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Burlingame</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 204.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1867-07-06"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi>
                            6, 1867.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your despatch of April
                    10th, No. 134, together with accompanying documents, namely, certain memorials
                    to the Chinese government and its replies on the subject of enlarged
                    institutions for scientific education. The proceedings described in these papers
                    are exceedingly interesting, and manifest a strong tendency on the part of the
                    imperial government toward assimilation to the institutions and customs of the
                    western nations.</p>
                <p>Trusting that you will lend your best exertions to favor this tendency,</p>
                <p>I am your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Anson Burlingame</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
